cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "AML-GraphMiner: an open-source toolkit for explainable money-laundering detection on transaction graphs"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-07  # TODO: set the real release date
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abeidak/aml-graphminer"
abstract: >-
  AML-GraphMiner is a modular Python toolkit that ingests financial transactions,
  builds transaction graphs, detects classical laundering motifs (fan-in, fan-out,
  cycles, scatter-gather, gather-scatter, smurfing) and risk communities, trains
  supervised Graph Neural Networks (GCN, GraphSAGE, GAT) and an unsupervised graph
  auto-encoder, and produces auditable explanations for every alert through a Python
  SDK, a web investigation interface, a command line and a REST API.
keywords:
  - anti-money laundering
  - graph neural networks
  - explainable AI
  - financial crime
